WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.290
Welcome to the Transhuman Daily, Tuesday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.550
Let's catch you up on the last 24 hours in transhumanism.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.230
One step at a time.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:21.090
A third blind volunteer got a brain implant aimed at restoring some sight.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:27.810
And a gene therapy for Huntington's disease now has an FDA decision date: May 1.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:37.010
In AI, OpenAI's new test grades everyday chores like budgets.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:39.270
Its best model scores 81%.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:39.990
Meanwhile,

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:45.490
a Neuralink user with ALS now steers his robot vacuum around the house just by thinking.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:47.430
In early results,

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:52.990
AI reading a wrist tracker and a pressure cuff flagged dangerous spikes up to 3 days early.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.990
And Meta reportedly built a home humanoid called Max in three months.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.250
It's not for sale.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.320
In the longevity lab,

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:06.680
dialling down one protein revved up cell recycling and cut Alzheimer's tau in flies.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.610
Another protein, MTR4, keeps blood vessel linings young.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.190
Boosting it let worms live longer.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:15.690
In people,

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:21.880
a study following 8,000 adults for 24 years linked extra weight to faster memory decline.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.500
And when Britain made kids stay in school a year longer,

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.430
dementia rates later fell slightly.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.890
For wellbeing,

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:36.530
the nonprofit Usona has reportedly filed psilocybin therapy for depression with the FDA.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.520
And in a small study of 40 women,

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:43.380
a brief bout of inflammation dampened their urge to socialise.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.300
Now, the catch. Five labs ran identical psilocybin tests in mice,

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:52.080
and the lasting effects didn't replicate.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.210
And a review of nine trials found little evidence

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.970
that medical cannabis helps people with insomnia.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.440
Meanwhile,

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:07.290
a former paratrooper just became the first person in Britain with a bionic upper arm.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:13.640
A Swiss implant turns surplus blood sugar into waste the body flushes out.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:14.830
So far, in mice.

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:20.540
And robots climbed 3,000 steps up China's Mount Tai, some carrying eggs.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.630
Implants, gene therapies, a bionic arm,

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:29.800
3,000 steps. The future arrives one step at a time.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.550
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.950
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.040
All of that, in one day. And the days keep getting bigger.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.340
That's the Transhuman Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.350
Go build the future. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
